  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For any $\\epsilon > 0$, there exist only finitely many triples $(a, b, c)$ of coprime positive integers with $a + b = c$ such that $c > \\text{rad}(abc)^{1+\\epsilon}$, where $\\text{rad}(n)$ is the product of distinct prime factors of $n$.",
